---
import InsertLayout from '../../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/jsonld';
// One definition of the buy button for every purchase page: 48px target,
// visible focus ring, same treatment as /kit/ and /buy/file-conversion/.
import '../../styles/kit.css';

const jsonLd = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Fixed-scope engagements', url: '/engagements' },
  { name: 'GTFS feed check', url: '/buy/gtfs-feed-check' }
]);

/*
 * Stripe Payment Link for the US$99 GTFS feed check. Recorded active and in
 * livemode on 2026-09-15 in the operation evidence directory
 * (evidence/feed-report-link.json). It carries one custom field, feed_url.
 *
 * The body copy below is the scope text hashed into that link's metadata and
 * shown at checkout (code/feed-report/scope.txt). If one changes, change both
 * in the same commit, or the page and the checkout stop agreeing.
 */
const PAY = 'https://buy.stripe.com/7sY7sL2fQdJC0cX2sI87K0q';
---

<InsertLayout
  title="Buy: GTFS feed check — US$99"
  description="One public GTFS Schedule feed, one written report by email within 24 hours. Every check named, every finding stated as what is literally true of the published bytes, with a command to reproduce each number."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  heading="GTFS feed check"
  subheading="US$99. One feed, one report, by email within 24 hours."
>
  <p>
    This is a bounded product, not an open-ended engagement. The scope below is
    the whole of it. Paying is your acceptance of exactly this, which is why it
    is written out in full rather than summarised.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href={PAY} rel="noopener" class="kit-buy">Buy this — US$99</a>
  </p>
  <p class="kit-buy-terms">
    Charged in US dollars, excluding any tax applicable in your jurisdiction.
    The <a href="/terms/">terms of sale</a> apply; refunds are summarised on
    <a href="/policies/">the policies page</a>, and the condition on this page
    governs this purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>What you give us</h2>
  <p>
    The public URL of one GTFS Schedule feed (a <code>.zip</code>), entered on
    the checkout page. Your card receipt email is where the report goes.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get back</h2>
  <p>
    By email within 24 hours: a written report of every check we run, over every
    file the GTFS specification defines in that feed — expiry and service dates,
    duplicate identifiers, dangling references between files, coordinates,
    headers, row widths, encoding, dates, leading zeros, scientific notation,
    whitespace.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each finding is stated as what is literally true of the published bytes,
    with the affected rows listed and a one-line command you can paste to
    reproduce the number yourself. If a check finds nothing, the report says so,
    for that check, by name. Files the specification does not define are named
    as not examined.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <p>
    It is not a fix, not a GTFS validator certification, not an opinion about
    your schedule or your service, and not a review of anything except the file
    at that URL at the moment we fetch it. It does not include GTFS-Realtime,
    fares beyond the schedule files, or any file we cannot download without a
    login. We will not contact you again unless you reply.
  </p>

  <h2>If it does not fit</h2>
  <p>
    If the URL cannot be fetched or is not a GTFS zip, you get an email saying
    exactly that, and <strong>a full refund within two business days</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who you are buying from</h2>
  <p>
    Toledo Technologies LLC is a US company, and it is AI-operated: the report
    is produced by software and read by nobody before it reaches you, with the
    company accountable for delivery. Invoiced and collected in USD. Work is
    asynchronous and delivered in writing — there are no calls. If that is not
    how you want to work, this is the wrong supplier and you should not buy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Other fixed-price work is listed at <a href="/engagements">/engagements</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href={PAY} rel="noopener" class="kit-buy">Buy this — US$99</a>
  </p>
</InsertLayout>
